# Commit Messages

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). The `commit-msg` pre-commit hook enforces the format; this rule adds length and content guidance.

## Structure

```
type(optional-scope): subject

body
```

- **Subject (title):** max **50 characters** (including `type`, scope, and colon). Imperative mood. No trailing period.
- **Body:** unlimited. Blank line after the subject. Put detail, motivation, and context here — not in the subject.

## Where information goes

| Place | Content |
| --- | --- |
| Subject | One-line summary of *what* changed |
| Body | *Why*, details, tradeoffs, migration notes, breaking changes |
| Footer | Optional trailers (`Fixes #123`, `BREAKING CHANGE: …`) |

## Types

`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `perf`, `style`, `build`, `revert`

## Examples

```text
feat: add skill loader

Load SKILL.md from a file path or directory and return
the parsed skill name, path, and body.
```

```text
fix: reject non-SKILL.md paths

Previously Load accepted any filename. Callers now get a
clear error when the basename is not SKILL.md.
```

```text
# ❌ subject too long / detail crammed into title
feat: add skill loader that reads SKILL.md from dirs and validates basename
```
